<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Legio XII Fulminata</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Twelfth Legion Fulminata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Legio XII Fulminata, the 'Thunderbolt' legion, was a Roman legion traced back to the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. From the later first century CE it was based at Melitene in Cappadocia, guarding the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> frontier. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domitian">Domitian</a> a detachment reached the Caspian and left a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobustan">Gobustan</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a>, the easternmost Latin inscription known.</p></div>
